<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">24 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 24 December, from 502 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">502 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,524 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Wu of Liang makes the infant Xiao Tong crown prince</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a>, founder of the Liang dynasty, made his one-year-old son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-tong">Xiao Tong</a> crown prince, having at first declined because the empire was not yet pacified. Xiao Tong later directed the compilation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wen-xuan">Wen Xuan</a>, but never reigned.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-liang">Emperor Wu of Liang</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiao-tong">Xiao Tong</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/971">971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,055 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jawhar al-Siqilli defeats the Qarmatians at the gates of Cairo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Fatimid general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawhar-al-siqilli">Jawhar al-Siqilli</a>, who had fortified Ayn Shams just north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> with a trench and wall, defeated the invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarmatians">Qarmatians</a> north of the city and forced them to withdraw from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in disorder.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawhar-al-siqilli">Jawhar al-Siqilli</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarmatians">Qarmatians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1144 CE <span class="tih-ago">882 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Imad al-Din Zengi captures Edessa from the crusaders</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege begun on 28 November, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imad-al-din-zengi">Imad al-Din Zengi</a>, atabeg of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, took Edessa, capital of the crusader County of Edessa, the first of the crusader states. Its fall prompted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-crusade">Second Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imad-al-din-zengi">Imad al-Din Zengi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1800">1800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon survives a bomb in the rue Saint-Nicaise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Royalist plotters exploded a barrel bomb in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> street as the First <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a>'s carriage passed, killing several bystanders but missing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. He used the attack to deport Jacobin opponents.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consul</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1814">1814 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Ghent ends the War of 1812</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and American negotiators signed a peace treaty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a>, restoring pre-war borders. News travelled slowly, and the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> was fought two weeks later.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1851">1851 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">175 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fire destroys much of the Library of Congress</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A fire in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitoline-hill">Capitol</a> destroyed about 35,000 of the Library of Congress's 55,000 books, including around two-thirds of the collection bought from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> in 1815.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1914">1914 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Christmas Truce begins on the Western Front</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Christmas Eve, soldiers along parts of the front sang carols across the lines. Over the next day many British and German troops met in no man's land, swapped gifts and buried their dead.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 8 orbits the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frank Borman, Jim Lovell and Bill Anders became the first people to orbit the Moon. They photographed 'Earthrise' and read from Genesis in a Christmas Eve broadcast seen by millions.</p></div></li></ol>
